# Pouliasis et al. (2024), A&A 685, A97  [arXiv:2401.13515]
# AGN X-ray luminosity function and absorption function in the Early
# Universe (3 <= z <= 6).
#
# Redshift bin: 5.0 <= z <= 6.0  (their highest-redshift binned data;
#     the 5.70-6.40 panel of their Fig. 10 shows only the model band).
# Band: rest-frame 2-10 keV, intrinsic (absorption-corrected).
# Column density range: 20 <= log NH <= 24.
# Cosmology: H0 = 70, Om = 0.3, OL = 0.7.
# Bins: 0.5 dex wide, tabulated at the bin centre.
# Phi convention: log10(dPhi/dlogLX / Mpc^-3 dex^-1).
#
# PROVENANCE: the paper plots these points in Fig. 10 but does not
#     tabulate them. The values below were recovered from the vector
#     coordinates of that figure in the arXiv source package (exact
#     marker and error-bar-cap positions), not by pixel digitisation.
#
# logLX  log_Phi  +dlog_Phi  -dlog_Phi
44.25 -5.982 0.36 0.50
44.75 -6.332 0.23 0.22
45.25 -6.790 0.15 0.15
45.75 -7.441 0.17 0.25
